    "customfield_12311020": null,
    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12348039/comment/12443660",
          "id": "12443660",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=steven_parkes",
            "name": "steven_parkes",
            "key": "steven_parkes",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Parkes",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Anybody worried about this? Seems like a very nominal change. Any reason we would want to inhibit people from extended a query class like FuzzyQuery? ",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=steven_parkes",
            "name": "steven_parkes",
            "key": "steven_parkes",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Parkes",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2006-10-19T22:41:56.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-10-19T22:41:56.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12348039/comment/12443946",
          "id": "12443946",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Making the class non-final is fine.\n\nAs far as changing members to protected, I'm not opposed to opening something up a little more so the very expert users don't have to copy the class (although that is often an option).  In return, those expert users shouldn't complain if the internals change ;-)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2006-10-20T21:27:57.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-10-20T21:27:57.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12348039/comment/12443952",
          "id": "12443952",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=steven_parkes",
            "name": "steven_parkes",
            "key": "steven_parkes",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Parkes",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Good point on the members.\n\nThere are public getter methods and the member are set from ctor, so the only reason for making them protected is to allow them to be set outside the ctor, right? Is that really necessary, to change them after construction?\n\nI have a tendency to prefer protected setters over protected fields, but there is precedence for this, e.g, BooleanQuery.minNrShouldMatch, so I don't think that part is exceptional.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=steven_parkes",
            "name": "steven_parkes",
            "key": "steven_parkes",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Parkes",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2006-10-20T21:50:54.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-10-20T21:50:54.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12348039/comment/12444708",
          "id": "12444708",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=steven_parkes",
            "name": "steven_parkes",
            "key": "steven_parkes",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Parkes",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "This version of the patch omits making the member variables public. FuzzyQuery is no longer final and some of the nested classes are made protected, but the member variables have getters so shouldn't need to be made public.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=steven_parkes",
            "name": "steven_parkes",
            "key": "steven_parkes",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Parkes",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2006-10-25T18:07:34.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-10-25T18:07:34.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12348039/comment/12444773",
          "id": "12444773",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=otis",
